WEBVTT

00:00:03.040 --> 00:00:05.460
<b>"Tokugawa Period"</b>

00:00:17.470 --> 00:00:19.760
<b>Government Certified Top Idols</b>

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:21.570
<b>Okita Soji</b>

00:00:21.570 --> 00:00:23.700
<b>Hijikata Toshizo</b>

00:00:33.590 --> 00:00:35.980
Hijikata-sama! You're so wonderful!

00:00:35.980 --> 00:00:38.280
Okita-sama! You're the best!

00:00:49.110 --> 00:00:52.290
For every set of Shinsengumi member pictures

00:00:52.290 --> 00:00:56.510
from troops one through ten you buy,

00:00:56.510 --> 00:00:59.080
you'll get concert lottery tickets!

00:00:57.360 --> 00:01:00.360
<b>Concert</b>

00:01:00.850 --> 00:01:03.650
The person with the most tickets 
will have an advantage!

00:01:03.660 --> 00:01:04.780
I'll take ten!

00:01:04.050 --> 00:01:06.120
It's only natural to buy ten or twenty at once!

00:01:04.780 --> 00:01:06.120
I'll take twenty!

00:01:06.120 --> 00:01:08.280
If I don't see Okita-sama perform live,

00:01:08.280 --> 00:01:10.420
there's no point to living in the capital!

00:01:10.420 --> 00:01:13.510
That's right! 
You have to hear their songs live!

00:01:17.530 --> 00:01:19.130
<b>Sakamoto Ryoma</b>

00:01:18.010 --> 00:01:19.140
Hey, girls!

00:01:21.680 --> 00:01:23.870
Listen to my song!

00:01:23.870 --> 00:01:24.920
What are you doing?

00:01:25.390 --> 00:01:27.620
Cutting the line for concert tickets.

00:01:27.620 --> 00:01:30.510
And making your weird shamisen screech.

00:01:30.510 --> 00:01:32.230
Er, This isn't a shamisen—

00:01:32.230 --> 00:01:35.320
Shut up. I can't hear Okita-sama's solo.

00:01:35.320 --> 00:01:36.700
Go away. Shoo, shoo.

00:01:36.980 --> 00:01:39.030
Shoo, shoo? What am I? A dog?

00:01:43.210 --> 00:01:46.480
Just listen to my song on—

00:01:52.170 --> 00:01:53.250
That's...

00:01:54.100 --> 00:01:55.090
...a guitar.

00:03:29.540 --> 00:03:32.980
<b>Peace Soul! Let's Rock!</b>

00:03:29.810 --> 00:03:32.980
Peace Soul! Let's Rock!

00:03:33.920 --> 00:03:35.990
Miss, more sake!

00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:36.180
<b>Di Telada</b>

00:03:35.990 --> 00:03:37.790
Where's our pizza?

00:03:37.790 --> 00:03:39.870
Coming!

00:03:40.230 --> 00:03:42.370
Hey, take it to their table!

00:03:42.370 --> 00:03:46.950
Here's Alberco di Telada's 
famous Pizza Margherita.

00:03:46.950 --> 00:03:49.940
So this is pizza. I've never had it before.

00:03:49.940 --> 00:03:51.300
How do you eat it?

00:03:51.300 --> 00:03:53.260
Well, sir...

00:03:54.390 --> 00:03:55.830
First, you cut it like this.

00:03:55.830 --> 00:04:00.330
Then you grab this part, roll it up, and...

00:04:00.330 --> 00:04:01.720
Don't eat that!

00:04:02.130 --> 00:04:05.000
All you have to do is explain it to them.

00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:08.210
If I send you out for deliveries, you get lost.

00:04:08.210 --> 00:04:10.100
If I have you wash dishes, 
you break them all.

00:04:10.100 --> 00:04:12.140
You really are useless.

00:04:13.640 --> 00:04:15.520
Go out back and do your job.

00:04:16.170 --> 00:04:18.230
What job?

00:04:18.230 --> 00:04:21.110
The only job you can do right.

00:04:21.820 --> 00:04:23.200
Good grief.

00:04:23.200 --> 00:04:25.060
Your dream of coming 
to the capital and becoming

00:04:25.060 --> 00:04:27.410
a successful musician is getting 
farther and farther away.

00:04:27.410 --> 00:04:29.450
Don't worry about that, Yataro.

00:04:29.450 --> 00:04:31.070
A respected master told me.

00:04:31.070 --> 00:04:33.310
My songs have passion.

00:04:33.310 --> 00:04:36.890
But Ryo-san, it's not easy for anything but

00:04:36.890 --> 00:04:41.900
the government's Heaven's Song 
to get approval in the capital or Edo.

00:04:41.900 --> 00:04:43.130
That's not true.

00:04:44.440 --> 00:04:48.230
My songs will be approved any day now!

00:04:48.890 --> 00:04:50.880
You're optimistic.

00:04:51.950 --> 00:04:53.300
I'm going out.

00:04:53.300 --> 00:04:54.090
What's this?

00:04:54.090 --> 00:04:56.090
Are you going to sing on the side 
of the road again tonight?

00:04:56.090 --> 00:04:58.400
Yeah, to convey my passion!

00:04:58.570 --> 00:04:59.880
See you later!

00:05:00.230 --> 00:05:02.900
You're just going to be 
barked at by dogs again.

00:05:03.140 --> 00:05:07.130
Tonight, I'll even move those dogs!

00:05:12.530 --> 00:05:15.370
Welcome back. Was everyone moved?

00:05:16.190 --> 00:05:18.080
They threw rocks at me.

00:05:18.320 --> 00:05:20.590
Were the dogs moved?

00:05:21.070 --> 00:05:23.450
They pissed on me.

00:05:25.340 --> 00:05:28.090
Why don't they understand my music?

00:05:30.440 --> 00:05:31.530
Sake, huh?

00:05:32.400 --> 00:05:34.370
I don't feel like drinking.

00:05:34.890 --> 00:05:36.270
Have this, too.

00:05:37.110 --> 00:05:39.270
Pizza Margherita!

00:05:42.990 --> 00:05:47.990
In this era, the government's warriors sing.

00:05:49.450 --> 00:05:55.700
Warriors used to wear swords 
and inspire fear in us common folk.

00:05:56.060 --> 00:05:59.980
Now they sing and dance 
and are highly sought after.

00:06:00.360 --> 00:06:03.960
The songs of warriors whose true 
occupation isn't music are everything.

00:06:04.410 --> 00:06:07.780
But I won't give up.

00:06:09.190 --> 00:06:11.390
That's the spirit, Ryo-chan.

00:06:11.390 --> 00:06:12.260
Yeah!

00:06:14.470 --> 00:06:15.640
It's strange.

00:06:15.640 --> 00:06:20.130
Your music just sounds like noise now, 
but when I look at you,

00:06:20.130 --> 00:06:25.810
I feel like it'll make me 
a lot of money someday.

00:06:25.810 --> 00:06:29.240
Yeah. I'll pay you back for taking 
me and Yataro in after we

00:06:29.240 --> 00:06:30.450
collapsed in the street.

00:06:30.730 --> 00:06:32.020
Besides,

00:06:32.950 --> 00:06:35.330
you look very delicious.

00:06:36.680 --> 00:06:41.400
<i>The capital sure is a dangerous place.</i>

00:06:42.060 --> 00:06:52.170
<i>The depths of my mind are 
directly stimulated by passion</i>

00:06:52.170 --> 00:06:53.800
<i>What is...</i>

00:06:53.800 --> 00:06:55.490
A shooting star.

00:06:56.770 --> 00:06:58.270
Wh-What's going on?

00:07:01.690 --> 00:07:04.940
Another dream about Katsurahama.

00:07:06.160 --> 00:07:09.720
<i>Until then, I sang alone.</i>

00:07:10.230 --> 00:07:13.950
<i>But since that shooting star fell,</i>

00:07:13.950 --> 00:07:19.660
<i>I wanted everyone to hear 
my songs and be recognized for them.</i>

00:07:20.340 --> 00:07:21.420
<i>That's right.</i>

00:07:21.420 --> 00:07:23.670
Listen to my music!

00:07:23.670 --> 00:07:25.500
Hear me shout!

00:07:26.300 --> 00:07:27.370
Shut up!

00:07:27.370 --> 00:07:30.060
The noise you're making is 
interfering with my business!

00:07:30.060 --> 00:07:33.780
My child can't fall asleep! 
You're a nuisance!

00:07:36.130 --> 00:07:38.400
I won't give up!

00:07:40.130 --> 00:07:42.310
Your guitar sounds pretty cool.

00:07:44.580 --> 00:07:47.190
Kid! You know this is a guitar?

00:07:47.690 --> 00:07:49.950
In Edo, they're all being 
confiscated by government

00:07:49.950 --> 00:07:51.700
officials as part of their guitar hunt.

00:07:52.060 --> 00:07:53.190
Where'd you get that?

00:07:53.190 --> 00:07:58.170
I got this from the shaggy 
master when I was in Tosa.

00:07:58.170 --> 00:07:59.660
Shaggy master?

00:07:59.950 --> 00:08:01.310
I don't know his name.

00:08:01.860 --> 00:08:03.880
Aside from my boss and Yataro,

00:08:03.880 --> 00:08:06.170
he was the first person 
to acknowledge my music.

00:08:07.460 --> 00:08:11.360
But there are only three 
people who understand it.

00:08:11.360 --> 00:08:12.420
It's four.

00:08:12.420 --> 00:08:13.370
Huh?

00:08:13.670 --> 00:08:16.330
Your music is passionate.

00:08:16.330 --> 00:08:18.810
Really? You really think so, kid?

00:08:19.100 --> 00:08:21.180
Yeah, I like it.

00:08:21.180 --> 00:08:24.490
You're discerning, you pretty little boy.

00:08:24.490 --> 00:08:27.310
All right! I'll sing for you!

00:08:27.310 --> 00:08:29.330
Ryo-san! Ryo-san!

00:08:29.330 --> 00:08:30.320
Yataro?

00:08:30.540 --> 00:08:32.650
Look at this!

00:08:32.990 --> 00:08:34.990
<b>"Heaven's Song"</b>

00:08:33.700 --> 00:08:34.990
Audition?

00:08:35.340 --> 00:08:38.320
The government's recruiting 
Heaven's Song singers.

00:08:38.320 --> 00:08:41.780
If you pass, the government 
will grant you permission to sing.

00:08:41.780 --> 00:08:43.810
I don't like Heaven's Song.

00:08:43.810 --> 00:08:44.900
Ryo-san.

00:08:44.900 --> 00:08:48.740
I refuse to sing songs I don't like.

00:08:48.740 --> 00:08:50.600
Think about it.

00:08:50.600 --> 00:08:52.530
If you're a government-approved singer,

00:08:52.530 --> 00:08:55.010
you can probably sing your own songs.

00:08:55.830 --> 00:08:56.890
My own songs?

00:08:57.210 --> 00:09:00.090
First, wait for an opportunity 
to sing on a major stage.

00:09:00.090 --> 00:09:02.770
Then deliver your music to the world.

00:09:04.140 --> 00:09:07.350
My own songs on a major stage.

00:09:08.100 --> 00:09:11.470
I get it! Then a lot of people 
would hear my music!

00:09:11.470 --> 00:09:12.650
That's right.

00:09:12.980 --> 00:09:15.630
All right! I'll go to this audition!

00:09:15.630 --> 00:09:18.560
Yataro, let's give the government a scare!

00:09:18.560 --> 00:09:20.580
That's the spirit, Ryo-san.

00:09:20.580 --> 00:09:25.290
But first, I'm going to sing 
a song for this pretty, young...

00:09:25.290 --> 00:09:26.500
Huh?

00:09:27.650 --> 00:09:29.340
Where'd he go?

00:09:30.140 --> 00:09:32.470
Let's go to the audition!

00:09:32.470 --> 00:09:33.630
Yeah!

00:09:36.220 --> 00:09:38.260
Ow! What was that for?

00:09:38.580 --> 00:09:42.340
You may not audition without an invitation.

00:09:42.340 --> 00:09:43.580
An invitation?

00:09:43.580 --> 00:09:45.410
Come back when you get

00:09:45.410 --> 00:09:48.270
an invitation from 
a Heaven's Song master or lord.

00:09:50.660 --> 00:09:52.580
An invitation, huh?

00:09:52.580 --> 00:09:54.460
Are you okay, Ryo-san?

00:09:54.460 --> 00:09:56.500
Yataro, where did you go?

00:09:56.500 --> 00:09:58.750
You looked like you were arguing, so I hid.

00:09:58.750 --> 00:10:00.490
You coward.

00:10:00.490 --> 00:10:16.260
<b>Audition Space</b>

00:10:01.020 --> 00:10:05.260
I don't know where to get an invitation.

00:10:05.260 --> 00:10:07.790
A master is a distinguished teacher.

00:10:07.790 --> 00:10:09.190
A distinguished teacher...

00:10:09.190 --> 00:10:11.290
Like the shaggy master!

00:10:11.290 --> 00:10:13.390
The guy who gave you your guitar?

00:10:13.390 --> 00:10:16.260
Yeah! He called himself 
a distinguished teacher!

00:10:16.640 --> 00:10:18.080
He's self-appointed.

00:10:17.760 --> 00:10:24.770
<b>Audition Space</b>

00:10:18.080 --> 00:10:20.620
He's still a distinguished teacher! 
Who cares if he's self-appointed?

00:10:20.620 --> 00:10:23.490
I'm gonna find him and get him 
to write me an invitation!

00:10:23.490 --> 00:10:27.230
Hey, wait. How are you going 
to find him in the capital?

00:10:27.230 --> 00:10:28.610
Good point.

00:10:31.760 --> 00:10:34.190
All right! It looks just like him!

00:10:34.190 --> 00:10:36.020
This is a person?

00:10:36.020 --> 00:10:38.190
I feel like he's too shaggy.

00:10:38.190 --> 00:10:41.100
No, he was this shaggy and cool.

00:10:41.100 --> 00:10:43.040
You think this is cool?

00:10:43.420 --> 00:10:45.450
We'll take this and look for him.

00:10:45.780 --> 00:10:47.120
I don't know.

00:10:47.620 --> 00:10:48.750
I don't know him.

00:10:49.120 --> 00:10:50.750
I've never seen him.

00:10:50.750 --> 00:10:52.630
This is him.

00:10:52.890 --> 00:10:56.230
He's a shaggy person, not broccoli.

00:11:06.340 --> 00:11:08.520
What's wrong? Do your stomachs hurt?

00:11:08.520 --> 00:11:10.830
We lost the concert lottery!

00:11:10.830 --> 00:11:11.810
Concert?

00:11:11.810 --> 00:11:13.670
The Shinsengumi concert!

00:11:13.670 --> 00:11:17.780
I used all my savings to buy twenty tickets, too!

00:11:17.990 --> 00:11:21.260
I spent all my money on forty tickets!

00:11:21.260 --> 00:11:23.630
I can't believe I lost!

00:11:23.630 --> 00:11:26.580
How unlucky.

00:11:26.580 --> 00:11:29.050
I wanted to hear Okita-sama sing.

00:11:29.050 --> 00:11:31.760
I wanted to watch Hijikata-sama play.

00:11:31.760 --> 00:11:34.880
He'll put on a concert for you.

00:11:34.880 --> 00:11:37.550
His music is cool.

00:11:37.550 --> 00:11:39.920
It's you, the discerning pretty boy!

00:11:39.920 --> 00:11:41.240
This guy?

00:11:41.240 --> 00:11:43.970
I heard him play before, 
but it was just loud.

00:11:43.970 --> 00:11:45.290
How rude.

00:11:45.290 --> 00:11:48.060
It's like... you call that Heaven's Song?

00:11:49.380 --> 00:11:51.770
My songs aren't Heaven's Song!

00:11:52.920 --> 00:11:54.110
What, then?

00:11:54.110 --> 00:11:55.290
What are they?

00:11:55.950 --> 00:11:58.320
My songs are my songs!

00:12:00.350 --> 00:12:02.700
Clear your ears and listen to this!

00:12:07.330 --> 00:12:08.410
What was that for?

00:12:19.670 --> 00:12:21.650
What are you doing?

00:12:21.650 --> 00:12:24.710
Where'd you get that guitar?

00:12:24.710 --> 00:12:28.660
Are you one of those guitar-hunting officials?

00:12:28.660 --> 00:12:32.960
No! Did you steal it? 
Take it? Plunder it? Filch it?

00:12:32.960 --> 00:12:33.920
What'd you say?

00:12:33.920 --> 00:12:36.900
You thief! What'd you do to Shoin-sensei?

00:12:37.440 --> 00:12:38.460
Bastard!

00:12:38.460 --> 00:12:39.750
Shinsaku.

00:12:39.750 --> 00:12:41.070
Who are you calling a thief?

00:12:41.070 --> 00:12:43.740
My name is Sakamoto Ryoma!

00:12:43.740 --> 00:12:45.850
And that guitar was a gift!

00:12:45.850 --> 00:12:46.910
Liar!

00:12:46.910 --> 00:12:47.780
I'm not lying!

00:12:48.050 --> 00:12:50.660
I'll beat the truth out of you, if I have to.

00:12:50.950 --> 00:12:55.150
I don't know who you are, 
but I won't let you call me a thief.

00:12:55.150 --> 00:12:55.920
Bring it on!

00:12:56.390 --> 00:12:58.360
You don't need to tell me!

00:12:58.360 --> 00:13:00.250
You've been saying nothing but that!

00:13:01.680 --> 00:13:03.310
What was that for?

00:13:03.310 --> 00:13:05.590
Shinsaku, calm down.

00:13:05.590 --> 00:13:06.940
Don't try to stop me, Katsura-san.

00:13:06.940 --> 00:13:08.220
I'll take this guy—

00:13:09.020 --> 00:13:10.970
I told you to calm down.

00:13:11.590 --> 00:13:14.230
Sorry for being so rough with you.

00:13:14.450 --> 00:13:18.480
That guitar belongs to 
our master, Yoshida Shoin.

00:13:18.770 --> 00:13:20.290
Your master?

00:13:20.290 --> 00:13:22.050
Don't act like you don't know him.

00:13:23.980 --> 00:13:26.990
You were asking around for him with this.

00:13:26.990 --> 00:13:29.050
This is definitely Shoin-sensei.

00:13:29.050 --> 00:13:31.860
It just looks like broccoli to me.

00:13:32.530 --> 00:13:36.790
Would you mind explaining how you 
came into possession of this guitar?

00:13:37.030 --> 00:13:39.100
How I got it?

00:13:39.540 --> 00:13:44.590
<i>Rolling lightning and flickering flashes</i>

00:13:40.720 --> 00:13:43.160
When I was singing in Tosa...

00:13:44.590 --> 00:13:47.390
Bravo! Impressive!

00:13:51.710 --> 00:13:52.770
Passion?

00:13:52.770 --> 00:13:57.540
That's right. Your songs have 
passion. A burning spirit.

00:13:57.540 --> 00:13:59.050
A burning spirit?

00:13:59.050 --> 00:14:00.520
You can have this.

00:14:02.660 --> 00:14:05.530
Play it with your soul.

00:14:05.720 --> 00:14:08.090
Believe in your passion!

00:14:08.090 --> 00:14:10.910
Your burning spirit!

00:14:11.210 --> 00:14:13.910
Passion? That means Shoin-sensei...

00:14:14.180 --> 00:14:17.660
He recognized your music as rock.

00:14:17.660 --> 00:14:19.920
Rock? What's rock?

00:14:20.230 --> 00:14:23.920
Rock is a new kind of music from the West.

00:14:23.920 --> 00:14:28.930
It's a rebellious musical style 
that stands against stereotypes.

00:14:28.930 --> 00:14:32.430
It's a wonderful music of passion and soul.

00:14:32.660 --> 00:14:34.620
My music is rock?

00:14:34.620 --> 00:14:37.180
What was that performance just now?

00:14:37.180 --> 00:14:39.680
That crappy music isn't rock!

00:14:39.680 --> 00:14:43.010
But Shinsaku, Shoin-sensei himself...

00:14:43.010 --> 00:14:46.370
Katsura-san, I refuse to accept this guy!

00:14:46.370 --> 00:14:48.930
My music is called rock.

00:14:48.930 --> 00:14:52.770
It's a passionate and soulful style that

00:14:52.770 --> 00:14:55.500
strongly opposes Western stereotypes.

00:14:55.500 --> 00:14:56.700
Isn't it great?

00:14:56.700 --> 00:14:57.690
Rock?

00:14:57.690 --> 00:14:59.810
Hey, listen to me!

00:14:59.810 --> 00:15:01.250
I know.

00:15:02.090 --> 00:15:04.590
Listen to my song!

00:15:07.010 --> 00:15:09.150
My samurai radar is responding.

00:15:09.150 --> 00:15:11.720
Another incomprehensible invention?

00:15:12.010 --> 00:15:14.270
You don't have to call it incomprehensible.

00:15:14.840 --> 00:15:15.970
Look, they're here.

00:15:16.460 --> 00:15:18.510
See? It's accurate.

00:15:19.000 --> 00:15:21.350
I just heard a guitar being played here.

00:15:21.350 --> 00:15:22.540
What? No way!

00:15:22.540 --> 00:15:25.950
Is that Shinsengumi Eighth Unit 
captain, Todo Heisuke-sama?

00:15:29.800 --> 00:15:32.570
You, there! That's a prohibited guitar!

00:15:33.440 --> 00:15:37.330
I don't know about your prohibition, 
but yeah, it's a guitar.

00:15:37.100 --> 00:15:42.070
<b>Heaven's Song</b>

00:15:37.580 --> 00:15:41.540
You were just playing something other 
than Heaven's Song with that guitar.

00:15:41.540 --> 00:15:42.960
Yeah! It's rock!

00:15:43.290 --> 00:15:45.460
That idiot. Answering 
his question honestly...

00:15:45.840 --> 00:15:47.500
I will confiscate your guitar!

00:15:47.500 --> 00:15:52.310
And I will arrest those who play 
music other than Heaven's Song!

00:15:48.110 --> 00:15:49.830
<b>Heaven's Song</b>

00:15:52.390 --> 00:15:53.870
What'd you say?

00:15:57.850 --> 00:16:02.200
This is the capital, not Edo. 
Aren't you going too far?

00:16:02.200 --> 00:16:04.860
Kyoto and Edo are nothing before 
the authority of the government.

00:16:05.550 --> 00:16:07.530
Well, we're here.

00:16:07.530 --> 00:16:10.360
Shoin-sensei was right to be worried.

00:16:10.640 --> 00:16:13.360
Shoin? Yoshida Shoin, huh?

00:16:13.820 --> 00:16:17.350
The government is trying to control 
the country with Heaven's Song.

00:16:17.350 --> 00:16:21.300
Most concert tickets go to the samurai 
class and wealthy merchants.

00:16:21.300 --> 00:16:23.280
Only a few go to commoners.

00:16:23.750 --> 00:16:25.330
Knowing this, you make them

00:16:24.020 --> 00:16:26.990
<b>Concert</b>

00:16:25.330 --> 00:16:30.020
use most of their money on concert 
lottery tickets to restrict their lives.

00:16:30.740 --> 00:16:32.510
You're well-informed.

00:16:32.840 --> 00:16:34.850
You dare voice an opinion 
against the government?

00:16:34.850 --> 00:16:35.880
Arrest him!

00:16:35.880 --> 00:16:38.420
You're just as guilty for 
listening! Arrest them!

00:16:38.420 --> 00:16:39.750
Hey, those girls have nothing to—

00:16:39.750 --> 00:16:41.850
Arrest me, arrest me!

00:16:41.850 --> 00:16:43.080
Am I dreaming?

00:16:43.080 --> 00:16:44.900
I'm being arrested by the Shinsengumi!

00:16:44.900 --> 00:16:46.460
I'll get to see Okita-sama!

00:16:46.460 --> 00:16:47.240
Whoa, whoa.

00:16:47.240 --> 00:16:49.690
Dissenters, come quietly!

00:16:50.480 --> 00:16:51.780
Run, guys!

00:16:53.740 --> 00:16:55.160
Idiot! You should run, too!

00:16:57.860 --> 00:16:59.540
I won't run.

00:16:59.900 --> 00:17:01.420
You've got guts.

00:17:01.420 --> 00:17:03.900
What's wrong with listening 
to the music I like?

00:17:03.900 --> 00:17:06.290
Music should be enjoyed freely!

00:17:06.920 --> 00:17:10.550
Music that restricts freedom isn't music!

00:17:10.940 --> 00:17:15.530
Rock won't be beaten by violence 
that restricts freedom!

00:17:17.870 --> 00:17:19.260
Well said.

00:17:19.750 --> 00:17:21.060
He's passionate.

00:17:21.330 --> 00:17:25.750
Music is free! It's the cry of our hearts!

00:17:27.150 --> 00:17:30.320
Action!

00:17:35.910 --> 00:17:40.950
<i>The depths of my mind are directly</i>

00:17:40.950 --> 00:17:46.210
<i>Stimulated by passion... What is this?</i>

00:17:46.210 --> 00:17:51.210
<i>A truth I've never experienced</i>

00:17:51.210 --> 00:17:55.920
<i>Is unmistakably burning</i>

00:17:56.140 --> 00:18:05.600
<i>I run, I stop, I get lost and sparks crackle and fly</i>

00:17:56.560 --> 00:17:57.960
That light...

00:17:57.960 --> 00:18:01.760
Is that the light of the Peace Soul 
Shoin-sensei told us about?

00:18:05.220 --> 00:18:08.490
Who is this guy? My body's on fire!

00:18:05.600 --> 00:18:11.670
<i>Adding the soul of sound to 
this voice and letting it fly</i>

00:18:08.490 --> 00:18:11.100
I won't let you leave me out!

00:18:11.670 --> 00:18:16.750
<i>Rolling lightning and flickering flashes</i>

00:18:16.750 --> 00:18:22.350
<i>Piercing a belief I cannot abandon</i>

00:18:22.350 --> 00:18:26.810
<i>Rolling thunder and unparalleled brilliance</i>

00:18:26.810 --> 00:18:32.780
<i>Composing a rolling no one can enter</i>

00:18:32.780 --> 00:18:38.240
<i>Hear this transcendent soul</i>

00:18:55.960 --> 00:19:00.690
<b>Nijo Castle</b>

00:18:56.810 --> 00:18:59.540
I have a message for the shogun!

00:18:59.540 --> 00:19:00.700
Please let me pass!

00:19:01.030 --> 00:19:04.320
The shogun hasn't been feeling well.

00:19:04.320 --> 00:19:06.170
I will make the report.

00:19:06.170 --> 00:19:08.760
But I was told to inform the shogun directly.

00:19:08.760 --> 00:19:09.830
The message.

00:19:10.680 --> 00:19:13.720
Do you have an objection 
to Chief Minister Ii Naosuke

00:19:13.720 --> 00:19:15.530
delivering the message?

00:19:15.530 --> 00:19:17.540
Please excuse me.

00:19:23.270 --> 00:19:24.640
Yoshinobu-sama,

00:19:25.270 --> 00:19:29.920
it seems men singing rock 
have appeared in the city.

00:19:29.920 --> 00:19:33.870
On top of that, they triggered the Peace Soul.

00:19:34.630 --> 00:19:36.980
But there is no need to worry.

00:19:37.550 --> 00:19:42.280
We have one of the Peace Souls.

00:19:44.460 --> 00:19:47.430
I heard it with my ears and felt it in my skin.

00:19:47.430 --> 00:19:51.120
Rock is amazing. It surpasses Heaven's Song.

00:19:51.670 --> 00:19:53.800
Let me speak with Kondo-san.

00:19:53.800 --> 00:19:56.030
Kondo-san is at the castle.

00:19:56.030 --> 00:19:59.980
Besides, there's no way Kondo-san 
would be interested in rock.

00:19:59.980 --> 00:20:01.130
But—

00:20:02.150 --> 00:20:03.760
If you don't stop complaining...

00:20:04.480 --> 00:20:05.260
...I'll kill you.

00:20:05.920 --> 00:20:08.060
Soji, don't.

00:20:08.820 --> 00:20:09.890
Hijikata-san.

00:20:11.510 --> 00:20:14.720
Todo, did you actually hear this rock?

00:20:14.720 --> 00:20:16.530
I did. So did my men.

00:20:16.530 --> 00:20:18.260
It's amazing.

00:20:18.260 --> 00:20:19.900
Shut up.

00:20:21.390 --> 00:20:23.360
Welcome back, Kondo-san.

00:20:24.250 --> 00:20:27.920
I received a message from 
Chief Minister Ii Naosuke-sama.

00:20:28.400 --> 00:20:29.820
A proclamation from the government

00:20:29.820 --> 00:20:31.370
will be issued soon in the capital, as well.

00:20:32.320 --> 00:20:34.080
It's almost time.

00:20:37.660 --> 00:20:38.420
Hey.

00:20:38.990 --> 00:20:40.430
What are you doing?

00:20:40.430 --> 00:20:42.170
Let's shake hands and make up.

00:20:42.170 --> 00:20:43.210
Now we're friends.

00:20:43.210 --> 00:20:43.930
What?

00:20:44.200 --> 00:20:46.960
I was moved.

00:20:46.960 --> 00:20:51.180
I had no idea how fun it was 
to rock out with like-minded friends.

00:20:51.420 --> 00:20:54.410
By friends, do you mean us?

00:20:54.410 --> 00:20:56.560
I don't accept this. I refuse to accept this.

00:20:56.770 --> 00:20:58.330
Now, now.

00:20:58.330 --> 00:21:00.570
Um... What are your names?

00:21:00.870 --> 00:21:03.110
I'm Katsura Kogoro.

00:21:03.110 --> 00:21:04.940
This is Takasugi Shinsaku.

00:21:05.970 --> 00:21:08.580
I see. Nice to meet you, Cindy.

00:21:08.580 --> 00:21:10.780
Who are you calling Cindy?

00:21:10.780 --> 00:21:13.430
Shinsaku sounds too refined.

00:21:13.430 --> 00:21:15.720
Don't you agree, Sensei?

00:21:15.720 --> 00:21:18.230
Sensei? You mean me?

00:21:18.230 --> 00:21:19.180
Yeah.

00:21:19.180 --> 00:21:20.960
Because you're smart.

00:21:21.300 --> 00:21:23.970
What a normal reason.

00:21:26.600 --> 00:21:30.280
I can make it with you guys. I know it.

00:21:30.280 --> 00:21:31.930
Let's rock together!

00:21:31.930 --> 00:21:34.770
I refuse to call your music rock.

00:21:34.770 --> 00:21:36.540
Don't be so upset, Cindy.

00:21:36.540 --> 00:21:38.190
Don't call me Cindy!

00:21:38.190 --> 00:21:42.200
The government will have 
their eyes on those who rock.

00:21:42.570 --> 00:21:43.990
Do you still want to do it?

00:21:44.270 --> 00:21:45.750
Of course.

00:21:45.750 --> 00:21:48.620
The government ain't nothing 
when you've got friends.

00:21:49.540 --> 00:21:54.230
Today marks the beginning of my...
our rock!

00:23:27.210 --> 00:23:33.350
I'm going to see a Top Idol Shinsengumi 
concert with Cindy and Sensei.

00:23:27.210 --> 00:23:35.970
<b>Top Idol! Rampage at a Concert!</b>

00:23:33.350 --> 00:23:36.740
In the next episode, 
I'll go on a rampage there.

00:23:35.970 --> 00:23:40.980
<b>Top Idol! Rampage at a Concert!</b>

00:23:36.740 --> 00:23:38.360
Don't miss it!

00:23:38.360 --> 00:23:40.980
You can watch it lying down if you want.
